WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.289 --> 00:00:04.846
(relaxing xylophone music)

00:00:06.046 --> 00:00:08.074
- I'm a little bit scared,
because I know that

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:10.255
Australia has animals that could kill me.

00:00:10.255 --> 00:00:12.246
- I've heard that kangaroos
are really strong,

00:00:12.246 --> 00:00:14.882
and they like to box,
and I'm very scared to

00:00:14.882 --> 00:00:16.878
meet an animal that knows how to box.

00:00:16.878 --> 00:00:18.317
I feel like this is gonna
be an Alice in Wonderland

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:19.944
type experience, in which I'm gonna

00:00:19.944 --> 00:00:21.604
go through the looking glass, and wind up

00:00:21.604 --> 00:00:23.705
somewhere that I don't even think is real.

00:00:23.705 --> 00:00:25.445
- I expect to lay on the ground and cuddle

00:00:25.445 --> 00:00:27.339
with at least three kangaroos.

00:00:27.339 --> 00:00:31.064
- This is real. This is really happening.

00:00:32.784 --> 00:00:34.313
We've just taken the ferry, and now

00:00:34.313 --> 00:00:36.274
we're about to go into
the sky to meet koalas.

00:00:36.274 --> 00:00:40.286
(funky rock music)

00:00:45.343 --> 00:00:46.736
- Oh my god!

00:00:48.046 --> 00:00:49.387
- They're all just chillin'.

00:00:49.387 --> 00:00:52.743
- [Girl] Holy shit,
literally just laying there.

00:00:52.743 --> 00:00:55.668
- [Guy] What an amazing union of animals.

00:00:55.668 --> 00:01:00.214
(upbeat rock music)

00:01:04.027 --> 00:01:05.885
I think I've found my spirit animal.

00:01:05.885 --> 00:01:07.869
I'm really into this echidna.

00:01:07.869 --> 00:01:09.484
Hi, Mia.

00:01:11.394 --> 00:01:12.782
- This is our baby quokka.

00:01:12.782 --> 00:01:13.992
- [Guy] Their numbers are declining

00:01:13.992 --> 00:01:15.079
because they're being hunted?

00:01:15.079 --> 00:01:17.066
- [Zookeeper] Because they
were being hunted originally,

00:01:17.066 --> 00:01:18.826
but now they're only
found on Rotness Isle,

00:01:18.826 --> 00:01:20.698
and they once were found
throughout Australia.

00:01:20.698 --> 00:01:22.352
- This is like, the perfect animal.

00:01:22.352 --> 00:01:23.652
I can't believe somebody would actually

00:01:23.652 --> 00:01:25.057
want to hunt this, this is like the most

00:01:25.057 --> 00:01:26.659
adorable thing I've ever seen in my life.

00:01:34.309 --> 00:01:35.634
This is bonkers.

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:37.040
Oh, hello.

00:01:37.501 --> 00:01:40.613
(pleasant guitar music)

00:01:43.742 --> 00:01:45.425
I can't believe you're real.

00:01:45.425 --> 00:01:47.062
- It looks like a stuffed animal. Oh!

00:01:47.062 --> 00:01:48.803
It's moving, oh my god!

00:01:48.803 --> 00:01:50.685
- [Guy] Oh, hi!

00:01:53.245 --> 00:01:56.375
- [Girl] It's so chill. It's
the chillest creature on earth.

00:01:56.375 --> 00:01:57.966
- [Guy] It's like all
of the stuffed animals

00:01:57.966 --> 00:01:59.916
from my childhood came alive.

00:01:59.916 --> 00:02:01.612
- I kind of feel like I'm still dreaming,

00:02:01.612 --> 00:02:03.794
like that didn't just happen.

00:02:03.794 --> 00:02:05.547
- I feel really changed.

00:02:05.547 --> 00:02:06.731
- I have a new dream job, and it's

00:02:06.731 --> 00:02:08.565
to be an Australian zookeeper.

00:02:08.565 --> 00:02:10.933
- A lot of animals, or even other places,

00:02:10.933 --> 00:02:13.627
you only think of them through TV or

00:02:13.627 --> 00:02:16.413
the Internet, or children's storybooks,

00:02:16.413 --> 00:02:18.257
and to actually be able to experience it

00:02:18.257 --> 00:02:20.209
was really, really special.

00:02:20.209 --> 00:02:21.717
- It's like, I'm gonna tell my children

00:02:21.717 --> 00:02:22.809
about this, someday, and they're

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:24.133
gonna be like, "No you didn't."

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:26.434
- [Guy] I still can't get over
that a quokka licked my cheek.

00:02:26.434 --> 00:02:28.599
- [Girl] I think my favorite
was for sure the quokka,

00:02:28.599 --> 00:02:31.024
because it's like a happy bunny rabbit.

00:02:31.024 --> 00:02:31.983
- [Guy] To be honest, it's

00:02:31.983 --> 00:02:33.671
gonna be hard to eat meat after this.

00:02:33.671 --> 00:02:35.330
- I would 100% come back here, like,

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:37.524
I wanna come back in an hour.

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:41.491
- [Guy] They're absolutely
beautiful, amazing creatures.

00:02:41.491 --> 00:02:43.108
Quokka is who you party with,

00:02:43.108 --> 00:02:45.070
kangaroo is who you hang out with,

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:47.172
and the echidna is a person that's

00:02:47.172 --> 00:02:48.925
a little bit too cool for you.

